🎧 Sonic Fusion - DJ Mixer Pro
​Sonic Fusion is a professional-grade, browser-based DJ mixing studio designed with an immersive cyberpunk aesthetic, advanced Web Audio API routing, dual-deck waveforms, 3-band EQs, custom crossfader curves, real-time DSP effects, and session recording capabilities.
​✨ Key Features
​Interactive Cover & Splash Screen: Features neon glowing buttons (Pré-escuta, Iniciar Mixagem, and Gravar) with smooth entry animations into the mixing console.
​Dual Deck Architecture (Deck A & Deck B): Independent track loading, playback, cue point setting, variable pitch/tempo control, and 4-second looping.
​WaveSurfer.js Integration: High-definition waveform visualization for precise track positioning and timeline monitoring.
​Real-Time Spectrum Analyzer: Dynamic canvas frequency visualizers responding instantly to audio output.
​Professional 3-Band Equalizer: Dedicated Low (shelving), Mid (peaking), and High (shelving) frequency control per deck powered by Web Audio API Biquad filters.
​Advanced Crossfader: Smooth mixing between Deck A and Deck B with selectable curve algorithms (Linear, Exponential, Logarithmic, and S-Curve).
​DSP Effect Rack: Instant application of Sweep filters, Reverb convolutions, and Delay echoes.
​Live Session Recorder: Capture your live DJ mix directly in the browser via MediaRecorder API and export as a .webm audio file.
​🚀 Getting Started
​No complex installation or build tools (like Node.js or Webpack) are required. Because Sonic Fusion is built as a Single-File Web Application, it runs entirely inside any modern web browser.
​Prerequisites
​A modern web browser with HTML5 and Web Audio API support (Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Microsoft Edge, or Safari).
​Running the Application
​Clone or download this repository.
​Open the index.html file directly in your web browser (double-click the file or drag and drop it into an open browser window).
​Click on "Iniciar Mixagem" on the splash screen to initialize the audio context and open the mixing console.
​🕹️ How to Use
​Load Tracks: Click on the upload area (Carregar MP3/WAV) in Deck A or Deck B to select local audio files from your device.
​Play & Monitor: Use the PLAY and PAUSE buttons. Use Set Cue and Go to Cue to manage cue points.
​Mix: Adjust individual track volumes, use the 3-band EQs to blend frequencies, and slide the Crossfader to transition between decks.
​Apply Effects: Select your target deck in the DSP Effect Rack and trigger Sweep, Reverb, or Delay.
​Record Your Mix: Click GRAVAR in the recorder panel to start capturing your audio session, then click PARAR to generate and download your .webm recording.
​🛠️ Built With
​HTML5 & CSS3: Styled with modern Tailwind CSS utilities and custom glassmorphism effects.
​JavaScript (ES6+): Core application logic and state management.
​Web Audio API: Low-latency audio routing nodes, filters, analysers, and stream destinations.
​WaveSurfer.js (v7): Interactive audio waveform rendering.
​FontAwesome & Google Fonts: Icons and typography (Orbitron & Inter).
